<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Kanmu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/737">737</a>–806</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Kanmu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanmu was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 781 to 806. To escape the influence of the Buddhist monasteries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a>, he moved the capital first to Nagaoka-kyō in 784 and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heian-kyo">Heian-kyō</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, in 794, beginning the Heian period. He also sent armies to subdue the Emishi of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-kanmu.jpg" alt="Emperor Kanmu" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Kammu_large.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
